# AGENTS.md

Rules for coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini CLI)
working in this repository. `CLAUDE.md` imports this file. Step-by-step
procedures for the common tasks are in `.agents/skills/` (see [Skills](#skills)).

## What this is

{{ name.title }}: a FastAPI **modular monolith** on Python {{ python_version }}, managed with **uv**,
SQLAlchemy 2 async on {{ database.label.split(" (")[0] }}{% if options.migrations %}, Alembic migrations{% endif %} and Pydantic v2.
Generated by [moarch-py](https://pypi.org/project/moarch-py/); the layout and rules
below are what moarch-py's commands assume.

## Commands

```bash
uv sync                                   # install from uv.lock
uv run fastapi dev src/{{ name.package }}/main.py   # run with reload
uv run pytest                             # all tests (in-memory SQLite, no server needed)
uv run pytest tests/modules/orders -k delete    # one folder, matching tests
uv run ruff format .
uv run ruff check --fix .
uv run mypy src
uv run lint-imports                       # modules talk only through public.py
{% if options.migrations %}
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<what changed>"
uv run alembic upgrade head
{% endif %}
moarch-py create module <name>               # a new module: public.py + every layer, registered
moarch-py create model <module> <name>       # another model in a module: class, schemas, repository, test
```

Add packages with `uv add <pkg>` (`--dev` for tools). Never `pip install`, and
never edit `uv.lock` by hand.

## Layout

```
src/{{ name.package }}/
  main.py               create_app(): settings, engine, middleware, routers
  core/config.py        Settings (pydantic-settings): the only place env vars are read
  core/errors.py        AppError and subclasses; the handler that maps them to HTTP
  core/logging.py       logging setup
  db/base.py            Base (naming convention), TimestampMixin
  db/session.py         engine, session factory, SessionDep
  db/repository.py      BaseRepository[Model]
  db/models.py          imports every model, for Alembic and the tests  (# moarch:models)
  api/health.py         /health, /health/ready
  api/v1/router.py      mounts every module router                    (# moarch:routers)
  modules/<name>/       public · models · schemas · repository · service · router · dependencies · mocks
tests/
  conftest.py           app / client / session fixtures on a fresh in-memory DB per test;
                        mock_client: an app with MOCK_RESPONSES on and no tables
  modules/<name>/       tests for that module
```

## Architecture rules

1. **Layers, and imports only go down:** `router → service → repository → session`.
   - `router.py`: HTTP only. Parse into a schema, call one service method,
     return a `Read` schema. No queries, no business rules.
   - `service.py`: business rules. Owns the transaction: **commits** when a
     unit of work is complete. Raises `AppError` subclasses, never
     `HTTPException`, and never imports FastAPI.
   - `repository.py`: the only place that builds queries. **Flushes, never
     commits.** Extend `BaseRepository`.
   - `dependencies.py`: builds repository and service from `SessionDep`, or
     the mock service when `MOCK_RESPONSES=true`.
   - `mocks.py`: sample data and `<Name>MockService`, a subclass of the
     service that answers from the samples and stores nothing, so a client
     can be tested before real data exists. **When you add a service method
     or a model column, update the mock too**; `test_<name>_mocks.py` covers it.
     Mock mode is refused in production.
2. **Modules talk to each other only through `public.py`.** A module is one
   business area (`orders`, `billing`); everything in it except `public.py` is
   private to it. Another module imports `modules/<name>/public.py` and nothing
   else there: not its models, repository, service or schemas module.
   `uv run lint-imports` enforces this (the contract is in `pyproject.toml`).
   - `public.py` hands out **schemas**, never SQLAlchemy models, and functions
     that take the caller's session and never commit.
   - Need something from another module? Add a function to *its* `public.py`.
     Never silence the contract with a new `ignore_imports` line.
   - A foreign key to another module's table is a string
     (`ForeignKey("orders.id")`), which needs no import. Never import
     `db/models.py` from a module: it imports every module.
3. **Schemas at the edge.** Endpoints accept `<Name>Create` / `<Name>Update`
   and return `<Name>Read` (or a page); never return a SQLAlchemy object or
   accept a `dict`.
4. **Errors** are `NotFoundError`, `ConflictError`, `PermissionDeniedError` or a
   new `AppError` subclass in `core/errors.py`, so every error has the same
   `{"error": {"code", "message"}}` shape.
5. **Configuration** is a field on `Settings` plus a line in `.env.example`.
   Never `os.environ` / `os.getenv` elsewhere, never a secret in code, never
   read `.env`.
6. **Async all the way:** `async def` endpoints, `await` every database call,
   no blocking I/O (`requests`, `time.sleep`) in a request.
7. **Types:** every function annotated; `uv run mypy src` stays clean. Models
   use `Mapped[...]` / `mapped_column`.
8. **Keep the `# moarch:` anchor comments** (also at the end of a module's
   `models.py`, `schemas.py` and `repository.py`). `moarch-py create` inserts above them.
{% if options.migrations %}
9. **Schema changes are migrations.** After changing `models.py`, autogenerate
   a revision, *read it* (autogenerate misses renames and some type changes),
   and commit it with the model change. Never edit an applied migration.
{% endif %}

### What this project adds

Rules for the parts `moarch-py` added on top (auth, security, tasks, services);
each guide is in `docs/`.

- **Settings for every part are on `Settings`**; read them from
  `request.app.state.settings`, never by calling `get_settings()` in a module.
